# cub kubara apply and handover on a live Kubara hub and spoke, on kind,
# 2026-09-28. See docs/user/cub-kubara.md.
#
# The platform: Kubara v0.15.0, bootstrap and general catalogs 3.0.0, one hub
# (lab-hub, stage dev) and one spoke (lab-spoke, stage prod: cert-manager,
# metrics-server, traefik). `kubara generate --helm` wrote it and
# `kubara bootstrap` installed Argo CD v3.5.2 on the hub, on kind v0.31.0 with
# Kubernetes v1.35.0. The hub delivered both clusters from a Git server in the
# hub cluster before this run. The ConfigHub side was a hosted organisation,
# with cub v0.6.2 and cub kubara 0.2.0-dev built from pull request #13.
#
# Known lab artefacts, present before the handover and after it: cert-manager
# is Degraded (the ACME email is example.com), traefik is Progressing (kind has
# no load balancer), and the argocd Application waits on an Ingress that never
# gets an address.
#
# apply.sh created 6 components and 10 variants. Handover took three runs. Run
# 1 left each Application reading Git: server-side apply added the ConfigHub
# source but kept Kubara's Git sources, which Kubara's bootstrap owns and Argo
# CD reads first. Run 2 fixed that and every Application stopped: Kubara's
# AppProject lists no sourceRepos (its Git is a project-scoped repository), so
# Argo CD refused the gateway, and the release that would permit it could not
# sync. Run 3 applied the AppProject first and every Application synced from
# ConfigHub. Each fix is in pull request #13, and re-running the script was
# safe each time.
#
# Then `cub kubara check` passed every variant Argo CD delivers. A change to metrics-server was
# promoted, approved and released to the dev cluster. check failed until Argo
# CD synced the new release, then passed, and the prod spoke stayed on its
# release. check --record wrote a LiveCheck attestation for each of them. A re-run
# of handover.sh with the released v0.2.0, while that change was only in dev,
# stopped before touching the hub; v0.2.1 fixes it. The change then went on to
# prod, and check passed both clusters on release 2.
#
# Commands ran with CUB_CONTEXT set to the hosted organisation and
# HUB_CONTEXT=kind-kubara-lab. Repeated promote progress lines are cut.

== cub kubara apply, live
$ cub kubara apply platform --out live --prefix lab \
    --capabilities lab-hub=kind-kubara-lab --capabilities lab-spoke=kind-kubara-lab-spoke
$ bash live/apply.sh

